Thank you Haakon. Gosh, could it be that simple? That, rather than the index vector, i, associated with the observation model correspond to each individual observation (i.e. 21 plots x 12 years = 252), it should have each index repeated for the number of plots per site. Hence, i=c(rep(1, 11), rep(2, 11)...rep(24, 10)), where 1 is transect 1, year 1 and includes the 11 plots in that transect and 24 is transect 2, year 12 and includes the 10 plots in that transect. As a result the lengths of the random effects "i" and "j" are 24, which is what I was expecting. As well, when I look at the fitted values, the first 11, which all come from the same year and transect, have similar values, and so on for each subsequent grouping. This would indicate a shared mean. (For these analyses, I dropped the "replicate" component). Is this correct?

